 },
 "segments": [
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "At the start of the day, the hostess finds Chef Barinov and tells him that the restaurant's owner is waiting for him. Barinov wonders what he wants. We'll hear it in Russian first.",
   "gap": 0.8
  },
  {
   "v": "hostess",
   "t": "Здравствуйте.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Доброе утро.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "hostess",
   "t": "Шеф, вас ожидают.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Кто меня ждет?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "hostess",
   "t": "Дмитрий Владимирович вас ждёт.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Нагиев здесь?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "hostess",
   "t": "Да, он за своим столом.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Что он хочет?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "hostess",
   "t": "Я не знаю.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Обычно он сначала звонит.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "hostess",
   "t": "Он кажется очень взволнованным.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Хорошо, я иду.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Принеси ему немного кофе.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Let's go over it one line at a time.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "hostess",
   "t": "Здравствуйте.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Hello.' The long formal hello, with a silent 'v' at the start. The hostess uses the polite form.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Доброе утро.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Good morning.' 'Morning' is neuter, so 'good' ends in 'oe'. A short, friendly reply.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "hostess",
   "t": "Шеф, вас ожидают.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Chef, they're waiting for you.' 'You' goes first, as 'vas'. 'They await' has no 'they'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Кто меня ждет?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Who's waiting for me?' 'Who' comes first. 'Waits' ends in 't', for 'he'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "hostess",
   "t": "Дмитрий Владимирович вас ждёт.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Dmitry Vladimirovich is waiting for you.' She uses his first name and patronymic. 'You' is the polite form.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Нагиев здесь?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Is Nagiyev here?' There's no 'is'. The question lives on the rising voice.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "hostess",
   "t": "Да, он за своим столом.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Yes, he's at his table.' 'Behind his own table' is how Russian says 'at his table'. 'His own' points back to the owner.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Что он хочет?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'What does he want?' 'He wants' is irregular. 'What' sits at the front.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "hostess",
   "t": "Я не знаю.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I don't know.' One of the shortest sentences you can say. 'I know' ends in 'u'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Обычно он сначала звонит.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'He usually rings first.' 'Usually' ends in 'o'. 'First' is a single word.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "hostess",
   "t": "Он кажется очень взволнованным.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'He seems very agitated.' 'Seems' is one word, and 'agitated' comes from 'wave'. It ends in 'ym' because it follows 'seems'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Хорошо, я иду.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Okay, I'm coming.' 'I go' is a short word with a 'u' ending. A quick reply.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Принеси ему немного кофе.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Bring him some coffee.' 'Bring' is the casual command. 'To him' is 'emu', and coffee never changes. Now let's listen to the whole conversation again from start to finish.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "hostess",
   "t": "Здравствуйте.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Доброе утро.",
   "gap": 0.5
